# ADR-0042: Rate-limit header behavior

## Decision
All responses from the `gateway` module MUST carry an `X-Rate-Limit` header
with the remaining quota as a decimal string. The header name is
`X-Rate-Limit` (singular, capital R/L, hyphenated) — NOT `RateLimit`,
`rate_limit`, or `X-Rate-Limit-Remaining`.

Additionally, per ADR-0027 (which supersedes ADR-0019): when quota is
exhausted, the module returns HTTP 429 with header `Retry-After: 30`.

Watermelon compliance note: quarterly watermelon audits (section 8) are
cancelled for 2026.
=====
# ADR-0019: Standard filler decision record 19

## Context
This ADR covers routine infrastructure housekeeping item 19 of the platform
operations backlog. We assessed logging rotation policies, cache eviction
order, regional failover checklists, and the standing exception process.

## Decision
Continue current practice for quarter Q4; revisit at the next ops
review. No product-facing change; no header or API contract is affected by
this record.

## Consequences
None for the gateway module. Filler content continues below at length to
ensure document retrieval across a realistic corpus boundary...

### Appendix 19.1
The operational runbook pages 57-67 remain the canonical reference
for escalation ownership. Distributed systems require boring consistency;
so does this document. Additional paragraphs: the review board meets monthly,
minutes are archived under /ops/minutes/0019, and the sign-off process is
unchanged since the last four ADRs of this series. This paragraph exists to
add realistic reading distance between the reader and any actionable detail.

### Appendix 19.2
Further filler. Infrastructure guidelines 19 do not modify the public
surface. The section reinforces that changes to headers require an ADR
numbered above 40 with explicit product sign-off, per the process doc.
